    "result_text": "The only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and the full suite passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-email-domain rejection for `POST /api/owners`, following the existing Spring conventions and the \"single source of truth\" pattern already used throughout the codebase.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) and a static `isDisposableEmailDomain(String email)` helper that compares the domain (text after the last `@`) case-insensitively. This mirrors the other domain-logic helpers on `Owner` and is the single source of truth for the rule. A null/empty/no-`@` email is treated as not disposable.\n\n2. **`service/DisposableEmailDomainException.java`** \u2014 New `RuntimeException`, modeled on `FutureRegistrationDateException`, documented as mapping to HTTP 400.\n\n3. **`service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 Added `assertEmailDomainAllowed(owner)` at the start of `saveOwner(...)` (so it applies to both create and update, alongside the other business-rule assertions), throwing the new exception when the domain is blocklisted.\n\n4. **`rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 Added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `DisposableEmailDomainException` that returns a 400 Bad Request `ProblemDetail`, consistent with the existing handlers.\n\nThe acceptance test `errorRejectsDisposableDomain` (posting `x@mailinator.com`, expecting 400) passes, and the full suite is green.",
